index e667ad8..a4acc7e 100644
--- a/docs/spec/radio-features.md
+++ b/docs/spec/radio-features.md
@@ -368,6 +368,43 @@ pre-emphasis reads 3 to 7 dB higher on the carrier than it is received. Measured
 None of them needs a correction in the driver. The HIL test (`test_fm_tx_dtmf`) checks the received twist;
 `test_fm_tx_dtmf_stop` checks on air that a held digit ends with the carrier at PTT release and at the time-out.
 
+### 3.8 MDC-1200 PTT ID (CONFIG_MDC1200; multi-mode derivative)
+
+An FM channel can identify itself with an MDC-1200 data burst when a transmission starts, when PTT is released, or
+both. The channel holds the settings (`open-firmware-cps.md` 7.3.3.2): the ID type (none, MDC-1200), when it is sent,
+and the 16-bit unit ID. There is no radio-wide ID: a channel with no ID sends nothing. Received bursts are not
+decoded yet; the channel's decode option is stored for it.
+
+The burst (`core/mdc/mdc1200.c`):
+
+| Part | Content |
+| --- | --- |
+| Line code | 1200 bit/s, one tone per bit: 1200 Hz when the bit equals the one before, 1800 Hz when it differs |
+| Preamble | 7 bytes 0x55 |
+| Sync | 07 09 2A 44 6F |
+| Data | 112 bits: op, argument, unit ID high and low, CRC low and high, 0, each bit followed (7 bytes later) by a parity bit over it and the bits 2, 5 and 6 before it; the 112 bits interleaved 16 apart |
+| CRC | CRC-16/CCITT, bit-reversed, start 0, inverted, over the first four bytes |
+| PTT ID | op 0x01; argument 0x80 at the start of a transmission, 0x00 at its end |
+| Length | 208 bits, 173 ms |
+
+The board sends it through `hal_afsk_t.tx_start` (1200 baud, mark 1200 Hz, space 1800 Hz), the sender APRS uses, so
+the switch needs `CONFIG_APRS`. The microphone is muted while a burst plays; the sub-audio tone stays on.
+
+| Rule | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| Start burst | after the carrier has been up 100 ms, 300 ms on a channel with a TX tone (the far squelch opens first) |
+| End burst | at PTT release, before the roger beep and the sub-audio tail. Only when the user lets go: not at the time-out or after a 1750 Hz burst |
+| Level | `hal_afsk_t` level 50 on a 25 kHz channel (the board's nominal, about 3 kHz peak), 25 on 12.5 kHz |
+| PTT released during the start burst | the burst is cut; the end burst (if set) follows |
+| PTT pressed again during the end burst | the burst is cut and the transmission goes on, with no second start burst |
+| DTMF | no digit while a burst is pending or on the air |
+| 1750 Hz burst | drops a pending or playing ID |
+| Host audio (USRP), hotspot | no ID |
+| Sender refuses or never ends | the transmission is an ordinary one; a burst still busy after 600 ms is stopped |
+
+With APRS built, the burst's 26 bytes of tones use the APRS transmit buffer: PTT has ended any APRS transmission, and
+none starts during one of ours. Untested on air: the pretimes and the 12.5 kHz level are first values.
+
